tool_definitions.description:
Reads a file from the local filesystem. Results are returned in cat -n format 
            with line numbers starting at 1: the prefix is spaces + line number + tab; 
            everything after the tab is the actual file content.


            By default reads up to 2000 lines or 50KB. Use `offset`/`limit` for long files; 
            when output is truncated a notice shows the kept lines and the next offset 
            to continue from.
